PHARMAKOS: THE SEALED ORDER - version @VERSION@, Windows x86_64
Build: @BUILD@

THIS BUILD IS UNSIGNED. If Windows SmartScreen says "Windows protected your
PC", choose "More info", then "Run anyway". Where Smart App Control is on, it
blocks an unsigned build and cannot be overridden for it.

Extract the whole zip before running anything, keep the files together, then
run Pharmakos.exe.

- If the lobby says the match host could not start, check whether antivirus
  quarantined gamectl.exe: the game starts it from this folder.
- The game needs a Vulkan-capable GPU (Godot's Forward+ renderer).
- Saves and the private match cache are in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Pharmakos. A save
  resumes only in a build with the same rules table and verifier as the build
  that wrote it. The remembered last match and the game's log are in
  %APPDATA%\Godot\app_userdata\Pharmakos.
- rules\ is not for editing: an edited rules.v1.json changes the rules hash, so
  older saves refuse to load, and it moves the host's Lull without the game's
  own countdown. library\ holds the templates the wizard and the built-in
  opponent read.

gamectl.exe, the command-line tool:
- Run it from this folder: "gamectl seat doctor" checks this install (all six
  checks pass here; from anywhere else pass --root <this folder>).
- "gamectl verify <file>" checks a playbook against gamectl's reference seat
  view, not your match. The live check when you submit in the game is the
  authority, so a file that places a beacon outside the reference view's
  spheres gets E0403 from the command line although the game accepts it.
- "gamectl --version" prints 0.0.0; the build line above identifies this build.

Licences: LICENSES\, REUSE.toml, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt and the game's Credits
screen. Changes: CHANGELOG.md.

Source: this build is commit @COMMIT@ of the game's repository (its public
address is set before a release is published). A release also carries the
tag's source archive on its release page.
